+      </section>
+      <section anchor="allocation" numbered="false" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.3">
+        <name slugifiedName="name-allocation">3. Allocation</name>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3-1">With respect to the allocation mechanism embodied in the ALL, GVB and
+RET commands, two alternatives were proposed:</t>
+        <ol spacing="normal" type="%c)" indent="adaptive" start="1" pn="section-2.3-2">
+          <li pn="section-2.3-2.1" derivedCounter="a)">make no change.</li>
+          <li pn="section-2.3-2.2" derivedCounter="b)">The flow control algorithm should be changed to keep track of
+two quantities: messages and bits.  The ALL, GVB, and RET commands
+each have two data fields.  The ALL command allocates a message
+limit and a bit limit.  The GVB command contains two fractions,
+and the RET command returns both messages and bits.  When sending
+a message, the sending NCP decrements its message counter by 1 and
+its bit counter by the text length of the message.  The sending
+NCP may not cause either of its counters to go negative.  The
+message counter would be 16 bits long.</li>
+        </ol>
